Description &amp; Requirements

Who we are looking for

We are looking for an experienced professional to join our team and contribute to a variety of advisory projects in the area of financial risk management for financial institutions.

We are looking for candidates who have:



- at least 3 years of professional experience in a bank, financial institution, lending company, supervisory authority or consulting firm, preferably in financial risk management, financial regulations, or quantitative risk modelling;
- strong analytical skills and a structured approach to problem-solving;
- a university degree, preferably in Economics, Finance, Mathematics, Econometrics, Computer Science, Quantitative Methods or a related field;
- experience or a strong interest in at least one financial risk area, such as credit risk, market risk, liquidity risk, interest rate risk, operational risk, or model risk;
- experience in working with and analysing data, particularly using Excel; knowledge of tools such as SQL, R, Python, SAS, VBA, or Matlab would be an advantage;
- an interest in quantitative models, data analysis, risk management processes, and financial sector regulations;
- willingness and openness to work with regulatory requirements, including Polish and European legislation as well as internal regulations;
- good command of English and Polish;
- strong communication and teamwork skills;
- independence and the ability to effectively organise your own work;
- willingness to learn and continuously develop your knowledge and skills.

Nice to have:



- experience in project management and/or coordinating the work of other team members;
- familiarity with and practical use of AI tools.

Your future role

As a Senior Consultant, you will participate in advisory projects for financial sector clients in Poland and across the Central European region.

Depending on your previous experience and areas of interest, you will have the opportunity to work on both quantitative projects, involving data analysis and modelling, and qualitative projects, focusing on risk management processes, regulatory requirements, and organisational aspects.

Your responsibilities will include:



- participating in projects across various areas of financial risk management, including credit, market, liquidity, interest rate, and model risk;
- conducting quantitative and qualitative analyses, including working with large datasets;
- developing, modifying, and validating risk models and methodologies;
- supporting risk identification, measurement, monitoring, and reporting processes;
- analysing regulatory requirements and supporting clients with their implementation and compliance;
- developing and testing tools and solutions supporting risk management, ALM and related processes;
- collaborating with clients and multidisciplinary teams, while sharing knowledge and supporting junior colleagues.

What we offer

What we offer:



- the opportunity to quickly gain practical knowledge and develop expertise across different areas of financial risk;
- participation in diverse projects for financial sector clients;
- opportunities to obtain professional certifications;
- collaboration with experienced professionals and the opportunity to build a strong industry network;
- a friendly working environment based on collaboration and knowledge sharing;
- opportunities to work with teams across different countries and locations and possibilities for short business trips;
- unlimited personal development opportunities (soft skills, programming courses, project management trainings, foreign language courses);
- attractive benefits package (Multisport card, life insurance, private medical care, access to a benefits platform, Employee Assistance Program, and more);
- opportunity to get involved in social and environmental initiatives, such as the Deloitte Foundation and Employee Networks: Parents, Proud, Neurodiversity, Multicultural, Gender Balance and others.

